            <ArticleTitle>[Proximal migration of a Double J catheter: case report and review of the literature].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>428-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To report one case of proximal migration of ureteral stent. To perform a bibliographic review about other cases and management to avoid this complication.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS/RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">48-year-old woman who presents right obstructive uropathy after gynecologic surgery. After the introduction of the right ureteral stent we observed a proximal stent migration. We put on a right nephrostomy tube and antergrade ureteral stent.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The right stent length and proper location of the distal tip are important factors to avoid this complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
